{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/MarkovText\/combine(_:weights:)","doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain\/combine(_:weights:)","doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain\/CombineError"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Advanced Usage","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/CustomizingSentenceSplitting","doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/PersistingModels"],"anchor":"Advanced-Usage"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/chainletter\/combiningmodels"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Blend multiple text sources to create hybrid generators.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ChainLetter allows you to combine multiple Markov models into a single generator. This is useful for blending writing styles, mixing topics, or creating weighted hybrids from different corpora.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Basic-Combination","text":"Basic Combination"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/MarkovText\/combine(_:weights:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to merge models:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let sciFi = MarkovText(sciFiCorpus)","let fantasy = MarkovText(fantasyCorpus)","","let blended = try MarkovText.combine([sciFi, fantasy])"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The combined model generates text that draws from both sources with equal probability.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Weighted Combination","type":"heading","anchor":"Weighted-Combination"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apply weights to control the influence of each source:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let formal = MarkovText(formalWriting)","let casual = MarkovText(casualWriting)","","\/\/ 75% formal, 25% casual influence","let mixed = try MarkovText.combine(","    [formal, casual],","    weights: [3.0, 1.0]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Weights are relative, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[3.0, 1.0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is equivalent to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[0.75, 0.25]"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[6.0, 2.0]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Combining-Multiple-Sources","text":"Combining Multiple Sources"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Combine any number of models:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let author1 = MarkovText(corpus1)","let author2 = MarkovText(corpus2)","let author3 = MarkovText(corpus3)","","let mashup = try MarkovText.combine(","    [author1, author2, author3],","    weights: [2.0, 1.0, 1.0]  \/\/ author1 has 2x influence",")"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Requirements-and-Constraints","text":"Requirements and Constraints","type":"heading"},{"type":"heading","text":"Same State Size","anchor":"Same-State-Size","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All models must have the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stateSize"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let model1 = MarkovText(text1, stateSize: 2)","let model2 = MarkovText(text2, stateSize: 3)","","\/\/ This throws Chain.CombineError.mismatchedStateSizes","let combined = try MarkovText.combine([model1, model2])"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Uncompiled Models Only","anchor":"Uncompiled-Models-Only","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Compiled models cannot be combined:"}]},{"code":["var model = MarkovText(corpus)","model.compile()","","\/\/ This throws Chain.CombineError.compiledChainNotSupported","let combined = try MarkovText.combine([model, otherModel])"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Combine models first, then compile the result if needed."}]},{"anchor":"Error-Handling","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Error Handling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"combine"},{"type":"text","text":" method throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain\/CombineError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for invalid inputs:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    let combined = try MarkovText.combine([model1, model2])","} catch Chain.CombineError.emptyModels {","    print(\"No models provided\")","} catch Chain.CombineError.mismatchedStateSizes(let sizes) {","    print(\"State sizes don't match: \\(sizes)\")","} catch Chain.CombineError.compiledChainNotSupported {","    print(\"Cannot combine compiled models\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"How-Combination-Works","type":"heading","text":"How Combination Works"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When models are combined, their transition counts are merged:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Model A: \"hello\" → [\"world\": 3, \"there\": 1]","Model B: \"hello\" → [\"world\": 1, \"friend\": 2]","","Combined: \"hello\" → [\"world\": 4, \"there\": 1, \"friend\": 2]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With weights, counts are multiplied before merging:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Model A (weight 2.0): \"hello\" → [\"world\": 6, \"there\": 2]","Model B (weight 1.0): \"hello\" → [\"world\": 1, \"friend\": 2]","","Combined: \"hello\" → [\"world\": 7, \"there\": 2, \"friend\": 2]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"level":2,"anchor":"Overlap-Checking-in-Combined-Models","type":"heading","text":"Overlap Checking in Combined Models"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When models are combined, their parsed sentences are also merged (if "},{"code":"retainOriginal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was true). This means overlap checking works against all source corpora:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let model1 = MarkovText(text1, retainOriginal: true)","let model2 = MarkovText(text2, retainOriginal: true)","","let combined = try MarkovText.combine([model1, model2])","","\/\/ Overlap checking works against both text1 and text2","if let sentence = combined.makeSentence() {","    print(sentence)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Combining-at-the-Chain-Level","type":"heading","text":"Combining at the Chain Level"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For lower-level control, combine ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain","type":"reference"},{"text":" objects directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let chain1 = Chain(corpus: corpus1, stateSize: 2)","let chain2 = Chain(corpus: corpus2, stateSize: 2)","","let combined = try Chain.combine([chain1, chain2], weights: [1.5, 1.0])","","\/\/ Create MarkovText from the combined chain","let model = MarkovText(chain: combined)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Use-Cases","type":"heading","text":"Use Cases"},{"text":"Blending Writing Styles","level":3,"anchor":"Blending-Writing-Styles","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a generator that mixes multiple authors:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let classicLit = MarkovText(dickensAndAusten)","let modernFiction = MarkovText(contemporaryNovels)","","let blended = try MarkovText.combine(","    [classicLit, modernFiction],","    weights: [1.0, 2.0]  \/\/ More modern influence",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Topic-Mixing","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Topic Mixing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Combine domain-specific corpora:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let techNews = MarkovText(technologyArticles)","let sportNews = MarkovText(sportsArticles)","","let newsBot = try MarkovText.combine([techNews, sportNews])"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Personality-Tuning","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Personality Tuning"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Adjust the “personality” of a chatbot by weighting different conversation styles:"}]},{"code":["let friendly = MarkovText(friendlyDialogue)","let professional = MarkovText(professionalDialogue)","let humorous = MarkovText(comedyDialogue)","","let chatbot = try MarkovText.combine(","    [friendly, professional, humorous],","    weights: [2.0, 1.0, 0.5]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/CombiningModels","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Combining Models","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ChainLetter"}]},"references":{"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter/Chain/combine(_:weights:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain\/combine(_:weights:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Combines multiple chains into a single chain with weighted transitions"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"combine","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"text":"Chain","preciseIdentifier":"s:11ChainLetter0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weights"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"Chain","preciseIdentifier":"s:11ChainLetter0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"combine(_:weights:)","url":"\/documentation\/chainletter\/chain\/combine(_:weights:)","type":"topic"},"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter/Chain/CombineError":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Error thrown when combining chains fails"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CombineError"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Chain.CombineError","url":"\/documentation\/chainletter\/chain\/combineerror","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CombineError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain\/CombineError"},"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Swift library for building Markov chain text generators."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter","url":"\/documentation\/chainletter","kind":"symbol","title":"ChainLetter"},"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter/Chain":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ChainLetter\/documentation\/ChainLetter\/Chain","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Chain"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Chain","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/chainletter\/chain","title":"Chain","abstract":[{"text":"A Markov chain representing a sequence model with explicit begin and end states.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Used to model processes like sentences that have natural beginnings and endings.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ChainLetter/documentation/ChainLetter/PersistingModels":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Save and load Markov models for later use."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Persisting M